---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="PIPL & China Data Export Compliance for AI Tools"
  description="China's PIPL and Data Security Law impose cross-border data transfer obligations on companies using AI tools. AI Privacy Gateway masks Chinese PII (ID cards, Unified Social Credit Codes, permits) locally and provides per-decision audit evidence for data-export assessment."
  keywords="PIPL数据出境,数据安全法AI,个人信息保护法,跨境数据传输合规,AI数据出境安全评估,统一社会信用代码脱敏,China data export compliance"
  canonicalURL="https://privacygw.pages.dev/pip-cross-border-compliance"
  ogType="article"
  hreflang={[
    { lang: 'en', url: 'https://privacygw.pages.dev/pip-cross-border-compliance' },
    { lang: 'x-default', url: 'https://privacygw.pages.dev/pip-cross-border-compliance' },
  ]}>
  <Nav />

  <section class="seo-page">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="seo-header">
        <div class="seo-badge">China Data Export Compliance</div>
        <h1>PIPL &amp; Data Security Law: Control AI Tool Cross-border Data Export</h1>
        <p class="seo-subtitle">
          When employees use Cursor, Claude Code, ChatGPT, and DeepSeek, source code, customer
          personal information, and internal data are transmitted to overseas servers — a cross-border
          data transfer. Under China's Personal Information Protection Law (PIPL) and Data Security
          Law (DSL), organizations must assess, classify, and retain evidence of such transfers.
          AI Privacy Gateway provides a locally-deployed technical control that makes AI data egress
          <strong>controllable, auditable, and provable</strong>.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="seo-tldr glass">
        <strong>In one line:</strong> AI Privacy Gateway masks Chinese PII (ID cards, Unified Social
        Credit Codes, HK/Macau/Taiwan permits, plates) locally before data leaves your network,
        classifies it as personal_info / important_data / core_data, and records per-transfer
        signed audit evidence — satisfying data-export assessment and record-keeping requirements.
        Deploy in 30 seconds, zero code changes.
      </div>

      <h2>Data Export Risks from AI Tools</h2>
      <div class="challenge-grid">
        <div class="challenge-card glass">
          <div class="challenge-num">1</div>
          <h3>Invisible Cross-border Egress</h3>
          <p>Developers use AI coding tools locally, sending source code, configs, logs, and customer data to overseas APIs. Security teams have no visibility into what data, when, and to whom.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="challenge-card glass">
          <div class="challenge-num">2</div>
          <h3>Unclassified Personal Information</h3>
          <p>PIPL requires personal information to be classified and protected by tier. Manual classification at scale is impractical.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="challenge-card glass">
          <div class="challenge-num">3</div>
          <h3>Important / Core Data Leakage</h3>
          <p>The DSL imposes stricter export controls on important and core data. Unified Social Credit Codes, business data, and customer lists can trigger security-assessment obligations.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="challenge-card glass">
          <div class="challenge-num">4</div>
          <h3>No Evidence to Prove Compliance</h3>
          <p>Without a gateway, you cannot prove that data was masked, what was exported, and to which overseas AI provider — a liability under regulatory inquiry.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <h2>How AI Privacy Gateway Solves It</h2>

      <h3>Local Masking with Deep Chinese-entity Coverage</h3>
      <p>The masking engine runs locally; data is replaced with placeholders before leaving the network. 26 entity types, with a focus on Chinese entities:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>China ID cards, phone numbers, bank cards (Luhn-validated)</li>
        <li>Unified Social Credit Codes, organization codes, business licenses</li>
        <li>HK/Macau/Taiwan permits, Taiwan IDs, resident permits, military IDs</li>
        <li>License plates (incl. new-energy), passports, API keys</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Automatic Data Classification</h3>
      <p>Every entity carries a compliance tier (<code>personal_info</code> / <code>important_data</code> / <code>core_data</code>).
      The highest-sensitivity tier of each request is stored in the vault, providing the classification
      basis for data-export assessment.</p>

      <h3>Per-decision Audit with Signed Evidence</h3>
      <p>Every request records team_id, source IP, target upstream, model, content hash, and per-entity
      detail (value hash only). SHA-256 hash chaining makes the trail tamper-evident, and
      <code>/admin/audit/export</code> exports a signed Ed25519 evidence bundle for regulatory
      record-keeping.</p>

      <div class="diagram-flow glass">
        <div class="diagram-row">
          <div class="diagram-node">AI Client<br/>(Cursor / Claude Code)</div>
          <div class="diagram-arrow">&rarr;</div>
          <div class="diagram-node diagram-accent">Privacy Gateway<br/>(mask + classify + audit)</div>
          <div class="diagram-arrow">&rarr;</div>
          <div class="diagram-node diagram-alt">Overseas AI API<br/>(placeholders only)</div>
        </div>
        <div class="diagram-row-sub">
          <span class="diagram-check">&#10003; PII stays in-network</span>
          <span class="diagram-check">&#10003; Export is recorded</span>
          <span class="diagram-check">&#10003; Classification is automatic</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <h2>Data Export Compliance Checklist</h2>
      <div class="checklist glass">
        <div class="checklist-item"><span class="check-icon">&#9634;</span><div><strong>Security assessment</strong><p>Classification and export statistics provide the technical basis for assessment filings.</p></div></div>
        <div class="checklist-item"><span class="check-icon">&#9634;</span><div><strong>Standard contract / certification</strong><p>Masked export drastically shrinks the data scope, lowering compliance cost.</p></div></div>
        <div class="checklist-item"><span class="check-icon">&#9634;</span><div><strong>Personal information classification</strong><p>Built-in three-tier auto-tagging (personal_info / important_data / core_data).</p></div></div>
        <div class="checklist-item"><span class="check-icon">&#9634;</span><div><strong>Export records &amp; evidence</strong><p>Hash-chained audit + Ed25519-signed evidence bundle for regulatory proof.</p></div></div>
      </div>

      <h2>Deployment</h2>
      <div class="code-block glass">
        <div class="code-block-title">Docker</div>
        <pre><code>docker run -d \
  --name ai-privacy-gw \
  -p 9999:9999 \
  -v ./vault_data:/app/vault_data \
  ghcr.io/gunxueqiu6/ai-privacy-gateway:lite</code></pre>
      </div>
      <p>Point your AI clients to <code>http://localhost:9999/v1</code>. Masking, classification, and audit happen automatically.</p>

      <div class="seo-cta">
        <h2>Make AI Cross-border Data Export Controllable, Auditable, Provable</h2>
        <p>Local deployment, 30-second setup, zero code changes. Enterprise adds audit export, longer retention, and multi-team.</p>
        <div class="seo-cta-buttons">
          <a href="/download" class="btn btn-primary btn-lg">Deploy Free</a>
          <a href="/demo" class="btn btn-ghost btn-lg">Live Demo</a>
          <a href="/pricing" class="btn btn-ghost btn-lg">Enterprise</a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <script type="application/ld+json">{
        "@context": "https://schema.org",
        "@type": "FAQPage",
        "mainEntity": [
          { "@type": "Question", "name": "Does masking remove data-export assessment obligations?", "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "Masking significantly shrinks exported data scope and lowers risk, but assessment triggers depend on data type and scenario — combine with legal counsel." } },
          { "@type": "Question", "name": "Which Chinese entities are covered?", "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "26 entity types including ID cards, Unified Social Credit Codes, HK/Macau/Taiwan permits, Taiwan IDs, military IDs, organization codes, plates, and bank cards." } },
          { "@type": "Question", "name": "Can it be deployed on-premise?", "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "Yes. Local deployment on bare metal, VM, Kubernetes, or Docker — data never leaves your network." } }
        ]
      }</script>
    </div>
  </section>

  <Footer />
</Layout>

<style>
  .seo-page { padding: 8rem 0 4rem; }
  .seo-page .container { max-width: 820px; margin: 0 auto; }
  .seo-header { margin-bottom: 3rem; }
  .seo-badge { display: inline-block; padding: 0.35rem 0.85rem; border-radius: 20px; font-size: 0.78rem; font-weight: 600; color: var(--primary); background: rgba(134, 239, 172, 0.08); border: 1px solid rgba(134, 239, 172, 0.15); margin-bottom: 1.25rem; }
  .seo-page h1 { font-size: 2.5rem; font-weight: 800; letter-spacing: -0.04em; line-height: 1.2; margin-bottom: 1.25rem; }
  .seo-subtitle { font-size: 1.05rem; color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.85; }
  .seo-subtitle strong { color: var(--text-primary); }
  .seo-tldr { padding: 1.25rem 1.5rem; margin-bottom: 2.5rem; font-size: 0.95rem; line-height: 1.7; color: var(--text-primary); }
  .seo-tldr strong { color: var(--primary); }
  .seo-tldr code { background: var(--bg-deep); padding: 0.15rem 0.4rem; border-radius: 4px; font-size: 0.85rem; font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; }
  .seo-page h2 { font-size: 1.7rem; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: -0.03em; margin: 3rem 0 1rem; padding-bottom: 0.5rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); }
  .seo-page h3 { font-size: 1.2rem; font-weight: 600; margin: 2rem 0 0.75rem; }
  .seo-page p { color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.85; margin-bottom: 1.25rem; }
  .seo-page ul { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin-bottom: 1.5rem; }
  .seo-page ul li { padding: 0.5rem 0 0.5rem 1.5rem; position: relative; color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.6; }
  .seo-page ul li::before { content: ''; position: absolute; left: 0; top: 0.9rem; width: 6px; height: 6px; border-radius: 50%; background: var(--primary); opacity: 0.5; }
  .seo-page a { color: var(--primary); text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 2px; }
  .seo-page code { background: var(--bg-deep); padding: 0.15rem 0.4rem; border-radius: 4px; font-size: 0.85rem; font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; }
  .challenge-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 1rem; margin-bottom: 2.5rem; }
  .challenge-card { padding: 1.75rem; }
  .challenge-num { font-size: 2rem; font-weight: 800; color: var(--primary); opacity: 0.5; margin-bottom: 0.5rem; line-height: 1; }
  .challenge-card h3 { margin: 0 0 0.5rem; font-size: 1.05rem; }
  .challenge-card p { margin: 0; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.7; }
  .diagram-flow { padding: 1.5rem; margin-bottom: 2.5rem; }
  .diagram-row { display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; gap: 0.75rem; margin-bottom: 1rem; }
  .diagram-row-sub { display: flex; justify-content: center; gap: 1.5rem; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .diagram-check { font-size: 0.88rem; color: var(--primary); font-weight: 500; }
  .diagram-node { padding: 0.6rem 1.25rem; border-radius: 10px; font-size: 0.85rem; font-weight: 600; background: rgba(134, 239, 172, 0.06); border: 1px solid var(--border); color: var(--primary); text-align: center; }
  .diagram-accent { color: var(--accent); background: rgba(167, 139, 250, 0.06); }
  .diagram-alt { color: var(--warning); background: rgba(251, 191, 36, 0.06); }
  .diagram-arrow { font-size: 1.25rem; color: var(--text-muted); }
  .checklist { padding: 1.75rem; margin-bottom: 2.5rem; }
  .checklist-item { display: flex; gap: 1rem; padding: 1rem 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); }
  .checklist-item:last-child { border: none; }
  .check-icon { font-size: 1.25rem; color: var(--primary); flex-shrink: 0; margin-top: 0.15rem; }
  .checklist-item strong { display: block; margin-bottom: 0.35rem; color: var(--text-primary); }
  .checklist-item p { margin: 0; font-size: 0.88rem; }
  .code-block { padding: 1.25rem; margin-bottom: 1.5rem; }
  .code-block-title { font-size: 0.78rem; font-weight: 600; color: var(--text-muted); margin-bottom: 0.75rem; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.06em; }
  .code-block pre { margin: 0; font-size: 0.85rem; line-height: 1.7; overflow-x: auto; }
  .code-block code { color: var(--primary); }
  .seo-cta { text-align: center; padding: 3rem 2rem; background: var(--glass-bg); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 20px; margin-top: 3rem; }
  .seo-cta h2 { margin-top: 0; border: none; }
  .seo-cta p { color: var(--text-secondary); margin-bottom: 1.5rem; }
  .seo-cta-buttons { display: flex; gap: 1rem; justify-content: center; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  @media (max-width: 768px) { .seo-page { padding: 6rem 0 3rem; } .seo-page h1 { font-size: 1.9rem; } .challenge-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } .diagram-row { flex-direction: column; gap: 0.5rem; } }
</style>
